---
functor: 1
title: taper
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`taper` · deform · make the start of the long axis thin, a tapered variant.

# Form

`x.taper` on a symbol, `(a + b).taper` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `to.wide.taper` | $to.wide.taper$ | built and cached |
| `mid.taper` | $mid.taper$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | Make the start of the long axis thin, a tapered variant. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A changed outline of the base. The compiler moves each point of the outline, and the strokes keep their shape and width. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.
- The start of the long axis goes to about one third of its size. On an arrow, the tail is thin and the head keeps its shape.

# From LaTeX

no LaTeX command.

